Hmm, there's not enough information to see what goes wrong. One guess
is that you might melee where throwing stuff from distance would give
you some advantage. Or that you let yourself get surrounded instead of
fighting in corridors or corners. Do you retreat if there seems to be
not much hope in a specific situation? Do you build up strong pets to
take some of the fighting burden from you? Do you pray if you are in
dire needs, or use Elbereth when appropriate? Do you escape situations
that likely evolve to be fatal? Use wands of digging and teleportation
(break the latter if you are surrounded), use level teleport to leave.

If you worry about AC, check every uncursed piece you find. If you want
to enchant it (scrolls have a base price of 80), wait to get a stack
and bless them all at once if you don't have enough holy water.

If you don't find and need an altar (for holy water and artifacts) you
may convert another altar; continue trying if the first tries does not
succeed. If there are only temples then a pet might help you to kill
the non-coaligned priest.

Maybe you want to give us some examples to get specific suggestions.

(If you have problems at approximately the same stage you might not
have considered every existing possibility. In critical situations
slow down in time and rethink about all your possible options.)

